Source bundle
-------------

spec/ and Assets/Sprites/Upstream/ were extracted, by tools/extract_spec.py, from the
blueprints_ui AssetBundle that Blueprints Included shipped at commit b1e3175
(dytterud/oni-mods, 2026-09-07). Git blob SHAs:

    windows  2335a6f7075235cb2eacb2f043159897236b639b   (the one extracted)
    mac      543411689ba7ff153668ffa72efbc1f16fa7ce85
    linux    4345a5e146bc65fafd0450a7bc068d163bb7b5ec

Those bytes are identical to SGT_Imalas' BlueprintsV2 at upstream commit e856903
(Sgt-Imalas/Sgt_Imalas-Oni-Mods, 2026-09-04), published under the MIT licence. Upstream
relicensed to All Rights Reserved at 771622f, 2026-09-07 21:57:24 UTC. That does not reach
back: the MIT grant attached to e856903 when it was published and is not retractable.
Nothing here comes from a later upstream revision. The evidence is in oni-mods'
docs/blueprints-included/asset-provenance.md.

What was taken from the bundle:

  spec/*.json
      The serialized state of the five prefabs Blueprints Included loads: hierarchy,
      component list and field values. blueprintInfoScreen, which nothing loads, was
      left out.

  Assets/Sprites/Upstream/*.png
      22 sprites the prefabs use that are not Oxygen Not Included's own art. They are
      carried under upstream's MIT grant. Where they came from before BlueprintsV2 is not
      recorded; some names (undo-2-xxl, parent_folder_icon_216194) suggest free icon sites.

What was not taken:

  Assets/Sprites/Game/*.png
      12 sprites the bundle embedded that are Oxygen Not Included's own art. Here they are
      plain white placeholders of the same size and border, under the same names.
      Blueprints Included swaps in the game's sprite by name at load, so no Klei art is in
      this repository or in the bundles it builds.

  Fonts
      The bundle embedded a NotoSans-Regular font and TMP font asset. Neither is needed:
      labels are converted to the game's own fonts at load. Text components here use
      Unity's built-in font, and TMP input fields carry no font asset.


